      "Note the observation window; a case without a period cannot be compared later. The record should show the source, the decision, and the surviving value in one place. Separate the request from the decision, because a complete request is not an approval. A short written rule is easier to test than an unwritten habit. The appeal deadline tracking record should let a second reviewer rebuild the decision from appeal deadline and appeal draft. Outsourced Billing Services keeps the appeal deadline tracking source, reviewer, and decision date together in the denial queue so a later check does not depend on memory.",
