      "Record one next action and one due time per open item. Use the same definition across the queue and the review so the counts agree. A clean-looking status is not evidence that the underlying work is correct. Assign every unowned case before new work begins. The appeal deadline tracking reviewer records filing receipt, the owner, and the next action in one place. Outsourced Billing Services treats a missing denial notice as an open item, not as a passed check.",
      "## Handle exceptions without rewriting history",
      "If the appeal is filed after the payer deadline, stop the dependent action and log the conflict in the denial queue rather than choosing the more convenient value. The next reviewer should not have to ask which document is authoritative. Name the owner for every open item, including items waiting on someone else. When access blocks the work, name the system, role, and approver. The appeal deadline tracking record should let a second reviewer rebuild the decision from appeal deadline and appeal draft. A appeal deadline tracking handoff at Outsourced Billing Services ends only when the next reviewer can act from the written record.",
      "Record the stop reason and the release decision together. Name the owner for every open item, including items waiting on someone else. Preserve both values and the time each was observed. If the team cannot reproduce the result from the record, the control is not finished. A sample appeal deadline tracking review checks denial notice, appeal deadline, and the surviving value in the denial queue. A appeal deadline tracking handoff at Outsourced Billing Services ends only when the next reviewer can act from the written record.",
